 the resulting C4 head. Do not fix the other-owner helper here or suppress the failure.\", \"reviewer\": \"rust-qa-agent\", \"severity\": \"important\"}, {\"category\": \"implementation-drift\", \"compliance_result\": \"non-compliant\", \"id\": \"CI-C4-001\", \"issue\": \"Inherited C3 process runner still calls stop_tree in timeout path and again in finally; POSIX termination is not idempotent and an OSError from finally can skip remaining process/pipe cleanup. The C4-specific idempotency correction does not repair this separate helper. CorrectivePR111 is not in e7.\", \"required_correction\": \"Consume C3 owner correction after QA/CI and rerun relevant independent helper regression checks. Keep inheritedID open until integrated; no waiver.\", \"reviewer\": \"req-qa\", \"severity\": \"Important\", \"source_refs\": [\".claude/project/quality-policy.md\", \"user zero-findings instruction\"], \"target_refs\": [\"scripts/runtime_templates.py:157\", \"scripts/runtime_templates.py:181\", \"scripts/runtime_templates.py:199\"]}, {\"adr\": null, \"description\": \"Inherited C3 template tooling still calls stop_tree in timeout handling and again in finally, with no one-shot ownership flag; an OSError from the repeated process-group termination can skip subsequent cleanup. CorrectivePR111 is not consumed by e7. C4 own runner correction does not repair this producer artifact.\", \"file\": \"scripts/runtime_templates.py\", \"id\": \"CI-C4-001\", \"line\": 199, \"remediation\": \"Consume the independently qualified C3 corrective parent and verify the affected helper gate. Retain producer ownership/ID; do not silently patch another sprint file or waive this Important finding.\", \"reviewer\": \"arch-qa\", \"rule\": \"RULE-GATE\", \"severity\": \"IMPORTANT\"}, {\"evidence\": \"Assigned e7 runtime_templates.py181 invokes stop_tree, timeout handling191 raises UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT, and finally200 calls stop_tree again without idempotency; stop_tree165-169 catches only ProcessLookupError, so PermissionError bypasses201-207 reap/close. Independent exact-source RustQA retained its controlled second-call denial result in rustqa-ci-c4-001.log. Corrective PR111 is not part of assigned HEAD.\", \"file\": \"scripts/runtime_templates.py\", \"id\": \"CI-C4-001\", \"issue\": \"The inherited C3 runner calls stop_tree in its timeout branch and unconditionally again in finally. A PermissionError from the second POSIX group signal masks the structured primary timeout and exits finally before child-reap and pipe-close code. This is the existing deterministic cleanup defect, not an intermittent startup timing failure.\", \"line\": 200, \"mechanism\": \"missing_reap\", \"recommendation\": \"Consume the C3-owned corrective PR through integration after its actual QA and CI pass; verify the one-shot termination, preserved original failure, real descendant cleanup and genuine initial-denial regressions on the resulting source. Keep this ID open at assigned e7; do not suppress EPERM or duplicate the producer patch in C4.\", \"reviewer\": \"flaky-test-qa\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"template runner timeout and final cleanup\"}], \"severity\": \"important\"}" .
